From 6eae122beebf992534220850c0d60d9fca858b59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:08:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: deliver deferred scan completion after
 shutdown

Interface shutdown completes cfg80211's scan request and retains its
netlink completion message for workqueue delivery. If the driver still
owns the request, its later completion only frees the stale request and
does not queue scan_done_wk. The retained message then keeps scan
admission busy across subsequent interface cycles.

Queue the existing worker whenever completion delivery is deferred.
Keep the current request ownership, direct delivery and split-scan paths.
The actual request-release, completion and worker functions reproduce
52 failures across 30 synthetic lifecycle cases before this change.
Workqueue, driver timing and message services are modeled; physical
wireless and concurrency acceptance remain open.

Port of Timothy Schmidt's original implementation
34c341b9039342611d3ca644a9aa9593bdad1c89. Original author and timestamp
are preserved. The original history credits Claude Opus 5.5 as co-author;
that original metadata is retained in the review evidence. This port,
changelog and qualification used OpenAI Codex assistance. Human review
and DCO certification remain pending.

Fixes: dab68a74e90b ("wifi: cfg80211: don't free driver-owned scan requests")
---
 net/wireless/scan.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/wireless/scan.c b/net/wireless/scan.c
index 1c50a16c0..34aece185 100644
--- a/net/wireless/scan.c
+++ b/net/wireless/scan.c
@@ -1194,10 +1194,18 @@ void ___cfg80211_scan_done(struct cfg80211_registered_device *rdev,
 	cfg80211_put_scan_req(rdev->scan_req);
 	rdev->scan_req = NULL;
 
-	if (!send_message)
-		rdev->scan_msg = msg;
-	else
+	if (send_message) {
 		nl80211_send_scan_msg(rdev, msg);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The interface is going down; defer the message to the worker.
+	 * A driver that still owns the request no longer queues the worker
+	 * when it completes, so do it here or new scans stay blocked.
+	 */
+	rdev->scan_msg = msg;
+	wiphy_work_queue(&rdev->wiphy, &rdev->scan_done_wk);
 }
 
 void __cfg80211_scan_done(struct wiphy *wiphy, struct wiphy_work *wk)
